-- posts
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000001', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000001', 'plants', 'GG4 week 5 of flower: the frost is coming in', 'Day 66 from sprout, day 35 since the flip. Running EC 1.8 in, runoff 2.1, pH 5.9. Switched to the bloom booster last week and the colas are stacking nicely.

RH is down to 48 % at lights on and 55 % at night, temps 25/20 °C. Planning to harvest around day 60 of flower and check trichomes from day 50.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000001/demo/flowering-early-bud.webp', 'https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000001/demo/flowering-trichomes-close.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000001', null, array['coco', 'led', 'gg4']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '28 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000002', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000002', 'question', 'Leaves pointing up and curling like a taco: too much light?', 'My Blueberry auto is on day 52. Since a few days the top leaves point up and the edges curl a bit. The LED is a 150 W board at 35 cm, dimmer at 100 %. Tent is 27 °C during the day. Is that light stress or heat? The rest of the plant looks happy.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000002/demo/nutrition-checking-leaves.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000003', jsonb_build_object('name', 'Bára', 'strain', 'Blueberry Auto', 'type', 'autoflower', 'stage', 'flowering', 'day', 52, 'dayInStage', 24, 'medium', 'soil', 'environment', 'indoor', 'lastWater', to_char(current_date - 1, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'lastFeed', jsonb_build_object('date', to_char(current_date - 4, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'ph', 6.4, 'ec', 1.3), 'notes', jsonb_build_array('Leaves pointing up at the top since day 49')), array['auto', 'soil', 'light']::text[], array['curl']::text[], now() - interval '14 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000003', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000003', 'harvest', 'Polytunnel Durban is down: 1.38 kg wet', 'The forecast said a full week of rain, so I took her down early. Trichomes were mostly cloudy with maybe 10 % amber, good enough for a sativa.

Whole plant is hanging upside down in the shed, 16–18 °C and around 60 % RH with a small fan for air movement (not pointing at the buds). Wet trim done, dry trim later. Will post the dry weight in about two weeks.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000003/demo/harvest-hanging-bud.webp', 'https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000003/demo/harvest-trimming.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000004', null, array['greenhouse', 'organic', 'harvest']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '60 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000004', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000009', 'question', 'How often should I water a two-week-old seedling in soil?', 'First grow here. My seedling is 14 days old in a 11 l pot of light mix. I water about 200 ml every day but the soil on top stays dark and wet. Is that too much? The leaves look fine so far.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000009/demo/seedling-sprout.jpg']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000011', jsonb_build_object('name', 'Amnesia #1', 'strain', 'Amnesia Haze Auto', 'type', 'autoflower', 'stage', 'seedling', 'day', 13, 'dayInStage', 9, 'medium', 'soil', 'environment', 'indoor', 'lastWater', to_char(current_date - 3, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'lastFeed', jsonb_build_object('date', to_char(current_date - 8, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'ph', 6.3, 'ec', 0.6), 'notes', '[]'::jsonb), array['seedling', 'soil', 'first-grow']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '74 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000005', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000007', 'gear', 'Quantum meter PPFD map of my 240 W bars at 30 cm', 'Finally borrowed a proper quantum meter. 120×120 tent, 4 bars, 240 W total at the wall, 30 cm above the canopy:

centre 980 µmol, mid ring 820–870, corners 610–650.

So the corners get about 35 % less. I moved the outer bars 10 cm towards the walls and the corners went up to 700 with the centre at 930. Small change, much more even canopy. Measure before you buy a bigger light!', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000007/demo/start-gear-tent.webp']::text[], null, null, array['led', 'ppfd', 'measurements']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '98 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000006', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000008', 'plants', 'Purple Kush day 45 of flower: living soil, water only', 'No bottles at all this run. The soil was mixed in spring (peat, compost, worm castings, pumice, a dry amendment mix) and I top dressed once at the flip.

Nights at 17 °C brought out the purple. Fading started on the lower fans this week, which is exactly what I want in week 7.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000008/demo/flowering-late-cola.webp', 'https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000008/demo/nutrition-late-fade.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000010', null, array['living-soil', 'organic', 'purple']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '124 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000007', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000006', 'harvest', 'First harvest ever: 41 g dry from one balcony auto', 'I can not believe it worked! Northern Lights auto, 97 days from seed on a south-west balcony in Prague. 160 g wet, 41 g dry after 10 days in the wardrobe with a small fan.

Things I learned: start earlier in the year, use a bigger pot (mine was 11 l) and do not panic about every yellow leaf at the end. Now curing in jars and burping them twice a day.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000006/demo/drying.jpg', 'https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000006/demo/jar.jpg']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000008', null, array['auto', 'balcony', 'first-harvest']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '380 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000008', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000005', 'problem', 'Yellow lower leaves in week 4 of veg: nitrogen?', 'White Widow in soil, day 27. The two lowest sets of leaves are turning pale yellow from the tips inwards, the top is still dark green. I water with pH 6.5 and gave grow nutrients at half strength once a week. Is she hungry or is it a pH problem?', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000005/demo/deficiency-nitrogen.jpg']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000007', jsonb_build_object('name', 'Widow', 'strain', 'White Widow', 'type', 'photoperiod', 'stage', 'flowering', 'day', 28, 'dayInStage', 0, 'medium', 'soil', 'environment', 'indoor', 'lastWater', to_char(current_date - 21, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'lastFeed', jsonb_build_object('date', to_char(current_date - 26, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'ph', 6.5, 'ec', 1.4), 'notes', '[]'::jsonb), array['soil', 'veg']::text[], array['yellowing']::text[], now() - interval '500 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000009', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000004', 'plants', 'DWC Lemon: roots after 10 weeks, still white', 'Lots of people asked how my roots look this late in a DWC. Here they are. Water at 19.5 °C with a small chiller, reservoir change every 7 days, EC 1.6, pH drifting from 5.7 to 6.1 between top ups.

Beneficial bacteria every reservoir change, no hydrogen peroxide.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000004/demo/media-hydro-roots.webp', 'https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000004/demo/media-hydro-buckets.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000006', null, array['dwc', 'hydro', 'roots']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '170 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000010', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000002', 'general', 'Hello from Ostrava! First grow, first post', 'Hi everyone, I just started my first ever plant. It is a Blueberry auto in a small 60×60 tent with a 150 W LED. I read the guide in the app twice and I am still nervous about overwatering. Nice to meet you all!', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000002/demo/seedling-led.jpg']::text[], null, null, array['first-grow', 'hello']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '1000 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000011', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000003', 'outdoor', 'Outdoor season wrap-up: Garden Skunk harvested', 'The garden Skunk #1 came down in mid September, 1.24 kg wet and 305 g dry after a slow two-week dry. Not a single spot of bud rot, even after a wet September. That strain is a tank.

ScrOG net outdoors worked great to keep the branches from snapping in the wind.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000003/demo/environment-outdoor-plant.webp', 'https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000003/demo/training-scrog-canopy.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000005', null, array['outdoor', 'organic', 'skunk']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '100 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000012', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000001', 'question', 'Runoff EC climbing to 2.6: flush or just feed lighter?', 'Coco, week 4 of flower. I feed EC 1.8 in and the runoff went from 2.0 to 2.6 in a week. Plant looks fine, no burnt tips yet. Should I do a big flush with plain water or just drop the input EC for a few feeds?', '{}'::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000001', jsonb_build_object('name', 'GG4 #2', 'strain', 'Gorilla Glue #4', 'type', 'photoperiod', 'stage', 'flowering', 'day', 57, 'dayInStage', 26, 'medium', 'coco', 'environment', 'indoor', 'lastWater', to_char(current_date - 9, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'lastFeed', jsonb_build_object('date', to_char(current_date - 9, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'ph', 5.9, 'ec', 1.8), 'notes', jsonb_build_array('Runoff EC 2.6 today')), array['coco', 'ec', 'runoff']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '218 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000013', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000007', 'gear', 'VPD for flower: what I actually run', 'Not the textbook chart, just what has worked in my tent for three runs:

week 1–3 of flower: 26 °C, 55 % RH, VPD about 1.2 kPa
week 4–6: 25 °C, 50 % RH, about 1.3 kPa
last two weeks: 22 °C, 45 % RH, about 1.4 kPa

A cheap hygrometer at canopy level matters more than an expensive controller on the wall.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000007/demo/environment-climate-hygrometer.webp']::text[], null, null, array['vpd', 'climate', 'flower']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '290 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000014', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000009', 'problem', 'Seedling stem is long and thin and falling over', 'My second seedling (a backup) got really stretchy, about 8 cm of thin stem with tiny leaves, and now it leans to one side. The light is about 60 cm above it. Can I save it?', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000009/demo/germination-stretched-seedlings.webp']::text[], null, null, array['seedling', 'first-grow']::text[], array['droop', 'slow']::text[], now() - interval '7 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000015', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000008', 'general', 'Top dressing in living soil: my schedule', 'Questions keep coming so here is what I do in a 50 l pot:

• transplant: amended soil, nothing else
• day 1 of flower: 2 cups of bloom amendment mix + 2 cups of worm castings, scratched in, mulch back on
• week 4 of flower: 1 cup of castings only

Water with plain dechlorinated water. Keep the mulch on and the soil never dries out completely. That is really it.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000008/demo/nutrition-healthy-leaf.webp']::text[], null, null, array['living-soil', 'organic', 'top-dress']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '335 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000016', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000005', 'plants', 'Flipped the Widow to 12/12', 'Day 42 from sprout and she is about 45 cm with eight tops after LST. Hoping for a stretch under 100 % in a 80×80 tent. Defoliated the inside a bit before the flip.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000005/demo/vegetative-untrained-plant.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000007', null, array['soil', 'lst', 'flip']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '142 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000017', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000006', 'question', 'Can autos handle a cold balcony at night (9 °C)?', 'My auto is in week 13, probably the last one, and the nights are getting down to 9 °C on the balcony. Should I bring it inside at night or will it be fine? Days are still 18–20 °C.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000006/demo/start-auto-vs-photo-cola.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000008', jsonb_build_object('name', 'Balcony NL', 'strain', 'Northern Lights Auto', 'type', 'autoflower', 'stage', 'curing', 'day', 91, 'dayInStage', 36, 'medium', 'soil', 'environment', 'outdoor', 'lastWater', to_char(current_date - 35, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'lastFeed', jsonb_build_object('date', to_char(current_date - 41, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'ph', 6.5, 'ec', 1.0), 'notes', '[]'::jsonb), array['outdoor', 'auto', 'cold']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '820 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000018', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000004', 'problem', 'Tiny speckles on fan leaves: mites?', 'Week 5 of flower in my DWC. A few fan leaves have tiny yellow-white speckles and I think I saw something moving under the leaf with my loupe. No webbing yet. How do I deal with this in flower without spraying the buds?', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000004/demo/spider-mites.jpg', 'https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000004/demo/problems-mites-macro.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000006', jsonb_build_object('name', 'DWC Lemon', 'strain', 'Super Lemon Haze', 'type', 'photoperiod', 'stage', 'flowering', 'day', 65, 'dayInStage', 30, 'medium', 'hydro', 'environment', 'indoor', 'lastWater', to_char(current_date - 10, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'lastFeed', jsonb_build_object('date', to_char(current_date - 10, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'ph', 5.8, 'ec', 1.5), 'notes', '[]'::jsonb), array['pests', 'hydro']::text[], array['spots', 'pests']::text[], now() - interval '245 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000019', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000002', 'plants', 'Bára started flowering', 'Day 31 and I see the first white hairs! She is about 29 cm, LST is keeping her flat. Really proud of this little plant.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000002/demo/vegetative-female-preflowers.webp', 'https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000002/demo/media-pots-plastic.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000003', null, array['auto', 'first-grow']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '500 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000020', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000007', 'plants', 'ScrOG net is in: Wedding Cake week 4', 'Topped once, then started tucking under a 5 cm net 25 cm above the pot. Flip when the net is about 70 % full, probably in 10 days. Coco, EC 1.4 in, pH 5.9.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000007/demo/canopy-scrog.jpg', 'https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000007/demo/training-topped-plant.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000009', null, array['scrog', 'coco', 'training']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '84 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000021', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000001', 'harvest', 'Northern Lights final numbers: 98 g dry from a 100×100', 'Single plant, 150 days from sprout including a long veg. 410 g wet, 98 g dry after 12 days at 18 °C and 58 % RH. Curing in jars at 62 %.

Next time: shorter veg, two plants instead of one. The tent was not full at the edges.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000001/demo/trichomes.jpg', 'https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000001/demo/harvest-curing-jar.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000002', null, array['coco', 'harvest', 'northern-lights']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '440 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000022', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000005', 'gear', 'Calibrate your pH pen more often than you think', 'My pen was off by 0.4 after only three weeks, which explains the weird leaves last run. I now calibrate every two weeks with 4.0 and 7.0 solutions and keep the tip in storage solution, never in tap water. Cheap pens are fine if you treat them right.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000005/demo/nutrition-ec-pen.webp']::text[], null, null, array['ph', 'gear', 'calibration']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '455 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000023', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000008', 'question', 'Fungus gnats after top dressing: anyone else?', 'Every time I top dress with worm castings I get a small wave of fungus gnats a week later. Not a disaster, but annoying. What do you use that is safe for a living soil?', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000008/demo/fungus-gnat.jpg']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000010', null, array['living-soil', 'pests']::text[], array['pests']::text[], now() - interval '620 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000024', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000003', 'general', 'Old grower tip: keep a written journal', 'Thirty years of growing and the best thing I ever did was writing everything down: date, water, feed, pH, weather, what I changed. You do not remember next season what you did this season. The diary in this app does exactly that, and the weekly updates make it easy to compare runs.', '{}'::text[], null, null, array['journal', 'tips']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '830 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000025', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000009', 'plants', 'My first plant just got its third node', 'Amnesia auto, day 9. Leaves look green and healthy (I hope). Watering only when the pot feels light, thanks for the tips in my other post.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000009/demo/germination-seedling-under-led.webp']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000011', null, array['first-grow', 'seedling']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '190 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000026', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000004', 'question', 'Chiller or frozen bottles for DWC in summer?', 'Last summer my reservoir hit 25 °C and I lost a plant to root rot. I can not afford a big chiller right now. Do frozen water bottles really work or is it a waste of time?', '{}'::text[], null, null, array['dwc', 'hydro', 'temperature']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '900 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000027', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000006', 'outdoor', 'Balcony auto in week 11: smell check', 'She smells sweet and earthy now and the buds are getting fat. Started watering a bit less and moved her where she gets the most sun in the afternoon.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000006/demo/flower-plant.jpg']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000008', null, array['balcony', 'auto']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '1000 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000028', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000002', 'problem', 'Brown crispy tips after feeding', 'Gave my auto its second feed (bloom nutrients, full dose from the bottle) and two days later the leaf tips are brown and crispy. Soil, pH 6.4. Did I overdo it?', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000002/demo/nutrient-burn.jpg']::text[], 'de3a0001-0000-4000-a000-000000000003', jsonb_build_object('name', 'Bára', 'strain', 'Blueberry Auto', 'type', 'autoflower', 'stage', 'flowering', 'day', 48, 'dayInStage', 20, 'medium', 'soil', 'environment', 'indoor', 'lastWater', to_char(current_date - 6, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'lastFeed', jsonb_build_object('date', to_char(current_date - 6, 'YYYY-MM-DD'), 'ph', 6.4, 'ec', 1.3), 'notes', '[]'::jsonb), array['soil', 'nutrients']::text[], array['burn']::text[], now() - interval '108 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000029', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000005', 'general', 'Weekly thread: what is in your tent this week?', 'Post a photo or a one-line update. I start: White Widow, day 6 of 12/12, stretch has started and she already grew 6 cm.', '{}'::text[], null, null, array['weekly']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '5 hours');
values ('de3a0002-0000-4000-a000-000000000030', 'de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000007', 'gear', 'Inline fan speed: why I run mine at 60 %', 'Bigger fan at lower speed is quieter and keeps the carbon filter happier than a small fan at 100 %. My 150 mm fan at 60 % keeps a 120×120 tent at 26 °C with 240 W of LED and negative pressure, so no smell leaks.', array['https://mlvpmiwvuxgwjssrtxsq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/de3a0000-0000-4000-a000-000000000007/demo/vegetative-veg-room.webp']::text[], null, null, array['ventilation', 'gear']::text[], '{}'::text[], now() - interval '510 hours');

